CAUTION: the animal-level totals are NOT comparable across the three
diseases. HPAI counts commercial poultry flocks (millions of birds per
year), rabies counts individually presented dogs and cattle, and
trypanosomosis counts herd-screened cattle. The denominators, the case
definitions and the detection pathways all differ. They are reported
per disease and must never be ranked against one another.

