TRYPANOSOMOSIS — reporting ends after 2021 and the last recorded value
(2021) is the series maximum. The WAHIS disease label itself is
'Trypanosomosis (tsetse-transmitted) (-2021)'; the '(-2021)' suffix marks
the end of the WOAH listing under that name, not the end of the disease.
The 2022 and 2023 blanks are therefore an ARTEFACT OF THE DISEASE
CLASSIFICATION, and are stored as missing, never as zero. Any statement
that trypanosomosis 'declined' or 'disappeared' after 2021 is unsupported.

