These two rankings measure different things and diverge. Cumulative
outbreaks are dominated by a few large HPAI epidemic semesters;
persistence reflects how consistently a state appears in the reporting
system. Both describe REPORTED SURVEILLANCE ACTIVITY. Neither is a
measure of disease risk: a state can report more because it has more
veterinary capacity, more commercial poultry, or a closer relationship
with the national reporting chain.

