==============================================================================
SENSITIVITY CHECKS
==============================================================================
S1. Withholding the Nassarawa -> Nasarawa recode:
    Nasarawa    {'Rabies': 0, 'HPAI': 12, 'Trypanosomosis': 3}
    Nassarawa   {'Rabies': 2, 'HPAI': 10, 'Trypanosomosis': 0}
    merged     {'Rabies': 2, 'HPAI': 22, 'Trypanosomosis': 3}
    Affects Nasarawa's own totals only; no state ranking above the top
    12 changes, and no disease-level or annual total changes at all.

S2. Effect of excluding the national ('Nigeria') rows:
    national outbreak rows in study period: 1, outbreaks = 1 (['HPAI'], [2014])
    national total incl. these = 2285; state-only total = 2284
    National rows are used for the national annual series (Phase 7) and
    excluded from all state rankings (Phases 8-9). They are never added
    to a state's total.

S3. Would summing every row double-count outbreaks?
    sum over ALL study-period rows        = 2285
    sum over outbreak (header) rows only  = 2285
    Identical, because detail rows carry '-' (NaN) for New outbreaks.
    Double-counting arises only if '-' is first converted to 0 and the
    animal columns are then summed alongside, or if a disease-year with
    no report is written in as a zero.

